# ─── MCP HTTP Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0

# ─── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RingCentral credentials are NEVER read from environment variables. Every
# /mcp request must carry them as HTTP headers instead (see README.md):
#   X-RingCentral-Client-Id
#   X-RingCentral-Client-Secret
#   X-RingCentral-Jwt
# This keeps per-tenant credentials isolated to the request that supplied
# them — no shared/global credential state on this server.
